# Template for infra/production/collector.env, which is NOT in git. Read by
# the collector service ALONE (A collector process, 2026-10-02;
# infra/production/README.md, The collector).
#
#   cp infra/production/collector.env.example infra/production/collector.env
#   chown root:root infra/production/collector.env
#   chmod 600      infra/production/collector.env
#
# The persona key seals every collection persona's credential (a Telegram
# session, a forum login). Only the collector holds it: the API, the sample
# origin, the cron loop, the Lab workers, the embedding pass and the egress
# proxy refuse to start if they find it. The database, the object store,
# Redis, the migration job and Caddy check nothing and all read secrets.env,
# so never copy it there. Generate it once:
#
#   python3 -c "import base64, os; print(base64.b64encode(os.urandom(32)).decode())"
#
# Lost, every persona must be enrolled again; nothing else is affected.
# Back it up with the database, somewhere that is not this host.
NOCTORNAL_PERSONA_KEK=replace-me

# The id recorded beside every credential the active key seals. Change it,
# with the old key moved to NOCTORNAL_PERSONA_KEK_RETIRED as
# persona:v1=<base64>, to rotate; scripts/rewrap_secrets.py --persona
# --apply then moves every credential under the new key.
# NOCTORNAL_PERSONA_KEK_ID=persona:v1
# NOCTORNAL_PERSONA_KEK_RETIRED=
